From e722c4f65d0abe3befea4fb1bc71bdc6f632ad53 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nathanial Fine <nathanial.fine@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 02:31:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Return the merged field in dst_layout when skip_deinterlace
 is set

After the circuit merge pass the merged image is transitioned to
READ_ONLY_OPTIMAL whenever a deinterlace pass is expected
(need_intermediate_pass), and only fastmad_deinterlace moves its output to
the caller's dst_layout. With VSyncInfo::skip_deinterlace the pass does not
run, so the caller received the field still in READ_ONLY_OPTIMAL and
FRAGMENT_SHADER scope while ScanoutResult promised dst_layout. A caller that
blits from it, as ICO's per-field (bob) presentation does, then blits from an
image in the wrong layout.

Add the missing barrier on the skip path. The non-interlaced path already
did the equivalent.
---
 gs/gs_renderer.cpp | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/gs/gs_renderer.cpp b/gs/gs_renderer.cpp
index e979198..5578b08 100644
--- a/gs/gs_renderer.cpp
+++ b/gs/gs_renderer.cpp
@@ -5105,6 +5105,16 @@ ScanoutResult GSRenderer::vsync(const PrivRegisterState &priv, const VSyncInfo &
 	{
 		for (auto &field : vsync_last_fields)
 			field.reset();
+
+		if (should_deinterlace)
+		{
+			// skip_deinterlace: the merged field was left in READ_ONLY_OPTIMAL for the
+			// deinterlace pass that is not going to run. Hand it back in the layout the
+			// caller asked for, the way the non-interlaced path does above.
+			cmd.image_barrier(*merged, VK_IMAGE_LAYOUT_READ_ONLY_OPTIMAL, info.dst_layout,
+			                  VK_PIPELINE_STAGE_FRAGMENT_SHADER_BIT, 0,
+			                  info.dst_stage, info.dst_access);
+		}
 	}
 
 	cmd.end_region();
